     --ww _f_i_l_e   Write the raw packets to _f_i_l_e rather than parsing and printing
               them out.  They can be analyzed later with the --rr option.
               Standard output is used if _f_i_l_e is ‘-’.

     --XX        Print each packet in hex and ASCII.  If the --ee option is also
               specified, the link-level header will be included.  The smaller
               of the entire packet or _s_n_a_p_l_e_n bytes will be printed.

     --xx        Print each packet in hex.  If the --ee option is also specified,
               the link-level header will be included.  The smaller of the en‐
               tire packet or _s_n_a_p_l_e_n bytes will be printed.

     --yy _d_a_t_a_l_i_n_k_t_y_p_e
               Set the data link type to use while capturing to _d_a_t_a_l_i_n_k_t_y_p_e.
               Commonly used types include EENN1100MMBB, IIEEEEEE880022__1111, and
               IIEEEEEE880022__1111__RRAADDIIOO.  The choices applicable to a particular de‐
